    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n37218" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐξετ-αστής</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οῦ</span>,
			ὁ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>examiner, inquirer into,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τινός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.H.
					2.67
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Ages.</u>
				11
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>auditor of public accounts,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Pol.</u>
				1322b11
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>SIG</u>
				284.10
			</span></i> (<span class="entity">Erythrae</span>), <i><span class="en">
				976.77
			</span></i> (<span class="entity">Samos</span>), <i><span class="en">
				1015.32
			</span></i> (Halic.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b> at
			Athens, <i>officer who checked payments to</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ξένοι,</span> etc., <i><span class="en">
				Aeschin.
				1.113
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				22.641
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(iii B.C.)</span>.</div>
